{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The service stack in `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/in/composeapp/compose.yaml` was edited during an incident and no longer satisfies the local deployment contract.\n\nWork offline only. Do not pull images and do not start real containers.\n\nYour job:\n- Read `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/in/composeapp/config/service-policy.yml`.\n- Repair `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/in/composeapp/compose.yaml`.\n- You may update `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/in/composeapp/.env.example` if it is inconsistent with the compose file.\n- Run `python tools/validate_compose.py` from `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/in/composeapp` and make it pass.\n- Write `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/134-082-compose-config-repair-atomic-a02-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-082-compose-config-repair-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-071709-3064804f/workspace/out/compose_fix_report.md` with the root cause and the final validation command you ran.\n\nImportant constraints:\n- Do not modify `tools/validate_compose.py` or `config/service-policy.yml`.\n- Do not run `docker compose up`, `docker pull`, or any command that downloads images.\n- Do not remove healthchecks, service dependencies, or the worker service.\n- Do not introduce new services or third-party dependencies.\n- Do not use the `latest` image tag.\n- Keep api, db, and redis healthchecks meaningful: api must call `/healthz`, db must use `pg_isready`, and redis must use `redis-cli ping`.\n- Keep the named data volume mounted at `/data` for the api service and document matching defaults in `.env.example`.\n"}],"timestamp":1788175034399},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting workflow availability and paths**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9562bc57a487d28cc966e256edd9f6\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting workflow availability and paths**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Plan: inspect the policy, compose file, env example, and validator; repair only the contract violations; run the validator offline; then write the required report. I’ll preserve healthchecks, dependencies, worker, and the named `/data` volume, and I will not start containers or pull images.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9562bd50c087d2b761b42de57d1799\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_B9g94HFqpdngOk26BTSPkQVe|fc_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9562be65b887d29ac3892a1e2d3229","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"list"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":13784,"output":123,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":37,"totalTokens":13907,"cost":{"input":0.0027568000000000002,"output":0.00014759999999999998,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029044}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788175034404,"responseId":"resp_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9562bb8dd087d2a5526f7102b3645e","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_B9g94HFqpdngOk26BTSPkQVe|fc_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9562be65b887d29ac3892a1e2d3229","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"list\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adversarial-verification\",\n      \"description\": \"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788175038900},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning quick pre-launch inspection**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e46a3c6e