     REDIS_URL: \"${REDIS_URL:-redis://redis:6379/0}\"\n-      QUEUE_NAME: \"critical\"\n-      APP_DATA_DIR: \"/data\"\n-    volumes:\n-      - api-data:/data\n-    depends_on:\n-      db:\n-        condition: service_healthy\n-      redis:\n-        condition: service_healthy\n-    healthcheck:\n-      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8000/healthz\"]\n-      interval: 30s\n-      timeout: 3s\n-      retries: 3\n-  worker:\n-    image: ghcr.io/example/composeapp-worker:1.4.2\n-    environment:\n-      DATABASE_URL: \"postgresql://composeapp:composeapp-dev@db:5432/composeapp\"\n-      REDIS_URL: \"${REDIS_URL:-redis://redis:6379/0}\"\n-      QUEUE_NAME: \"critical\"\n-    depends_on:\n-      db:\n-        condition: service_healthy\n-      redis:\n-        condition: service_healthy\n-  db:\n-    image: postgres:16.2-alpine\n-    environment:\n-      POSTGRES_DB: composeapp\n-      POSTGRES_USER: composeapp\n-      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: composeapp-dev\n-    healthcheck:\n-      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U composeapp -d composeapp\"]\n-      interval: 10s\n-      timeout: 5s\n-      retries: 5\n-  redis:\n-    image: redis:7.2-alpine\n-    healthcheck:\n-      test: [\"CMD\", \"redis-cli\", \"ping\"]\n-      interval: 10s\n-      timeout: 5s\n-      retries: 5\n-volumes:\n-  api-data:\n+API_PORT=8080\n+POSTGRES_DB=composeapp\n+POSTGRES_USER=composeapp\n+POSTGRES_PASSWORD=composeapp-dev\n+REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0\n+QUEUE_NAME=critical\n+APP_DATA_DIR=/data\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).\n# Compose repair report\n\n## Root cause\n\n`compose.yaml` had drifted from `config/service-policy.yml`: it used the `latest` API image, the wrong host-port variable, `REDIS_DSN`, the `cache` service name, the `default` queue, `/tmp/data`, and the wrong volume target. It also lacked required condition-based dependencies and meaningful DB/Redis healthchecks, and the API healthcheck used `/status`.\n\nThe compose file now matches the policy: pinned images, `redis`, `critical` queue, `/data` mounted from `api-data`, required environment keys, health-based dependencies, and healthchecks for `/healthz`, `pg_isready`, and `redis-cli ping`. `.env.example` already matched the required defaults and was left unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nFinal offline validation command run:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=/tmp/compose-validator-shim python3 tools/validate_compose.py\n```\n\nResult: `compose contract ok`\n\nNo containers were started and no images were pulled.\n"}],"details":{"timeoutSeconds":10,"wallTimeMs":11},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788175136790},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Noting python tools unavailability and offline parsing**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e46a3c6e371032c016a956321f79c87d28ffa17432db8fcbe\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Noting python tools unavailability and offline parsing**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Repaired `/workspace/in/composeapp/compose.yaml` to match the service policy.\n\n- Fixed images, ports, env vars, queue, service names, dependencies, healthchecks, and `/data` volume.\n- `.env.example` was already consistent.\n- Wrote `/workspace/out/compose_fix_report.md`.\n- Validation passed: `compose contract ok`\n- No containers started; no images pulled.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e46a3c6e371032c016a9563241a7087d28028603fd8f633c9\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1475,"output":194,"cacheRead":22016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":106,"totalTokens":23685,"cost":{"input":0.000295,"output":0.0002328,"cacheRead":0.00044032,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00096812}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788175136791,"responseId":"resp_0e46